# --- managed build output --------------------------------------------------
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
AppPackages/
BundleArtifacts/
*.appxupload
*.appxsym

# AppPackages is build output: every build writes a new .appx, its signing .cer and a copy of the
# VCLibs dependency, so tracking it would add megabytes of binaries per version. It is ignored, not
# deleted - build.bat clean leaves it alone, so previous builds stay on disk to sideload from.
#
# It does mean a fresh clone has no signing certificate. That is by design: the .pfx is a private key
# and is never committed, so a clone generates its own with make-cert.ps1 and installs that .cer on
# the phone once. Keep a backup of the .pfx somewhere outside the repo - it is the only thing that
# can sign an upgrade for an already-installed copy of this app.

# The vendored OpenSSL DLLs live in a folder called "bin", which [Bb]in/ above would swallow - a
# clone would then have the import libraries but no DLLs and could not package. Git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the directories themselves must be
# un-ignored here.
!/lib/openssl/wp81-arm-v120/bin/
!/lib/openssl/wp81-x86-v120/bin/

# --- native component output ------------------------------------------------
# A C++ project writes to <Platform>\<Configuration>\ (and, for Win32, straight to
# <Configuration>\), NOT to bin\ or obj\, so the rules above miss it entirely - this is ~100 MB.
# Paths are anchored to the Tls project so they cannot swallow lib\openssl\, which is vendored and
# IS tracked.
/src/GCalendarSync.Tls/ARM/
/src/GCalendarSync.Tls/Win32/
/src/GCalendarSync.Tls/x86/
/src/GCalendarSync.Tls/Debug/
/src/GCalendarSync.Tls/Release/
/src/GCalendarSync.Tls/Generated Files/

# --- linker / compiler artefacts, wherever they land -------------------------
# Belt and braces: the anchored rules above cover today's output paths, but a new configuration or
# platform would write somewhere they do not match. These extensions are never source.
#
# *.lib is DELIBERATELY ABSENT - lib\openssl\**\*.lib are the vendored OpenSSL import libraries
# and MUST stay tracked. Do not add it.
*.exp
*.ilk
*.obj
*.pdb
*.idb
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.tlog
*.pch
*.res
*.winmd
*.lastbuildstate
*.recipe
*.metagen

# --- Visual Studio noise ----------------------------------------------------
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.aps
ipch/

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# A real account file, if one is left in the repo while testing. The .sample in docs\ is the
# template and IS tracked. This is the only thing here worth keeping out.
gcalendarsync.cfg

# The package signing key is deliberately NOT ignored - see the note in README.md. It is a
# self-signed sideloading certificate for a test app that will never reach the Store, and tracking it
# is what lets any clone build a package the phone accepts as an upgrade of the installed app instead
# of a different one. Same arrangement as the Windows 10 Mobile version this was ported from.
